      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Take a Virtual Tour here (copy and paste the line into your browser):\r\nhttps://view.ricoh360.com/35f1ca68-e8e7-4dc0-beb4-a8b645d653e9\r\n\r\nKW Team Castles are pleased to present Cul Na Mara, Old Court Park, Bray, new to the Market.\r\n\r\nThis one/two bed, end-of-terrace home comes to the market in immaculate order throughout and boasts a number of notable features, including off street parking for up to two cars.\r\n\r\nThis beautifully presented modern home combines warm, inviting tones with a clean contemporary finish throughout. Thoughtfully upgraded, it offers bright living spaces, a well-designed kitchen, and cosy, stylish bedrooms that make the home feel both elegant and comfortable. Beyond its aesthetic appeal, the house is enhanced with a comprehensive Zigbee smart-home network that offers exceptional security and convenience. It includes multiple motion sensors throughout the ground floor, first floor, kitchen, and bedrooms, along with door and window sensors on the front door, back door, and key bedroom windows. \r\n\r\nThe property also features smart light switches and two dedicated Zigbee repeaters for strong, reliable coverage in every room. This system provides enormous potential for future automation, allowing the next owner to customise lighting, heating, security, and daily routines exactly to their preference. The sensors can also be used as a flexible whole-home alarm system, fully adaptable to however the new owner wishes to configure it. All devices run locally through a central hub, offering a fast, private, and future-proof smart-home foundation already built into the house.\r\n\r\nThe location here is second to none within minutes walk of Bray Main Street, all amenities and services are virtually on this property's doorstep including a wide selection of highly regarded schools including St Patricks National School, St. Cronans, Presentation College, Loreto College Bray, St. Gerards and the new North Wicklow Educate Together Secondary School. \r\n\r\nUCD, Belfield is easily accessible via the E1 bus route every 10 to 5 minutes while Bray is also home to its own Institute of Education. This family friendly location is just 20 kilometres south of Dublin City Centre, and the M50 is less than a kilometre away providing easy access to all surrounding areas. Bray is a wonderful seaside town with spectacular promenade and seaside boarding a lively bustling town with a range of services and amenities that are accessible to all."
      }
